    "content.about-story": [
     {
      "heightPx": 1113,
      "widthPx": 390,
      "topPx": 2113,
      "position": "static",
      "text": "I HAD TO LEAVE HOME TO BUILD A BETTER LIFE So I picked up and left home for the promise of a better future, open to wherever that would lead me. I swapped sweltering Louisiana sunshine for the frigid temps of north Chicago, then the predictability of San Francisco’s foggy mornings, and, later, New York City’s gritty, fast-paced vibe. I seized every single opportunity I could to learn, to try to get myself ahead of the game. I tried to emulate the qualities I admired most about my managers: the ones that felt most like the Southern kindness fed to me just as often as my mother’s gumbo back home",
      "structure": {
       "headings": [
        {
